OL,3,GNEWSAResidents say 'terrible smell' is
OL,4,Agetting worse
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents in Netherfield have said a
OL,7,F"terrible sewage smell" in the area has
OL,8,Fgot worse, despite repeated complaints
OL,9,Fto local authorities.
OL,11,FLocals blame a nearby sewage works and
OL,12,Fa pet food factory, saying the odour
OL,13,Fhas been affecting the area for years,
OL,14,Fbut has become stronger and more
OL,15,Ffrequent in recent months.
OL,17,FDr Seyi Awoku, who moved to Netherfield
OL,18,Feight months ago, has found the smell
OL,19,Fso bad he would not have moved if he
OL,20,Fhad known about the problem.
OL,23,APub: 27-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,369,360,200,160,0,100
